        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(voice-call): fix telnyx streaming transcription stt in conversation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\nInbound Telnyx PSTN calls went silent because Telnyx requires an explicit `POST /v2/calls/{call_control_id}/actions/streaming_start` command to start WebSocket media streaming. Additionally, Telnyx WebSocket frames are structured differently than Twilio frames, and were not being correctly parsed.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Technical Changes\r\n\r\n1. **`providers/telnyx.ts`**: Supported classic `streamPath` configurations, public URL storage, and stream URL resolution.\r\n2. **`manager/events.ts`**: Injected the classic `streamUrl` into `answerCall` parameters for Telnyx inbound calls (bypassed if realtime is enabled).\r\n3. **`media-stream.ts`**: Added support for pluggable WS message parsers and implemented `parseTelnyxMediaMessage()` to decode Telnyx inbound WebSocket frames.\r\n4. **`runtime.ts`**: Registered `parseTelnyxMediaMessage` and configured streaming options when initializing Telnyx.\r\n5. **`cli.ts`**: Updated self-check CLI output logic.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\nVerified locally by running the comprehensive unit test suites:\r\n- `telnyx.test.ts` (21/21 tests passed)\r\n- `media-stream.test.ts` (24/24 tests passed)\r\n- `events.test.ts` (20/20 tests passed)",
